n-names>MW</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldstein</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dopamine sulphate: an enigma resolved</article-title><source>Clin Exp Pharmacol Physiol</source><year>1999</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>S41</fpage><lpage>S53</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Clin Exp Pharmacol Physiol||26|S41||bib9|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gehm</surname><given-names>BD</given-names></name><name><surname>McAndrews</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Chien</surname><given-names>PY</given-names></name><name><surname>Jameson</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Resveratrol, a polyphenolic compound found in grapes and wine, is an agonist for the estrogen receptor</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>1997</year><volume>94</volume><fpage>14138</fpage><lpage>14143</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Proc Natl Acad Sci USA||94|14138||bib10|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gignac</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bourquin</surname><given-names>LD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of resveratrol and sulindac on intestinal tumor numbers in Min mice</article-title><source>FASEB J</source><year>2001</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>A630</fpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'FASEB J||15|A630||bib11|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goldberg</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Yan</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Soleas</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Absorption of three wine-related polyphenols in three different matrices by h